#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_gudermannian

#% text
# `inverse_gudermannian(x)` gives the inverse Gudermannian function 2 atanh(tan(x/2)).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `inverse_gudermannian(gudermannian(x)) = x` for real x.

#% item
# `inverse_gudermannian` is odd.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_gudermannian(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
inverse_gudermannian(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.226191170883517

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% cell
gudermannian(inverse_gudermannian(0.7))
#% output
#= 0.7

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `gudermannian`, `atanh`, `tan`
